<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">René Magritte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1898">1898</a>–<a href="/years/1967">1967</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">René Magritte was a Belgian surrealist painter whose witty images questioned the relation between pictures, words and reality. His works include &quot;The Treachery of Images&quot;, with its pipe captioned &quot;This is not a pipe&quot;, and &quot;The Son of Man&quot;, a man in a bowler hat whose face is hidden by an apple. He worked mainly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a> and influenced pop art and conceptual art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rene-magritte.jpg" alt="René Magritte" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_en_buste_du_peintre_surr%C3%A9aliste_Ren%C3%A9_Magritte_(1898-1967)_le_18_octobre_1961_devant_une_de_ses_toiles,_PH19994.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
